A two-bus grid: three generators, one line, three snapshots of rising demand.
validated: 2 buses, 3 generators, 1 line, 3 load rows given

solved: objective 1500.00, generation 270.0 meets load 270.0

generation by unit
  cheap    150.0
  peak       0.0
  wind     120.0
line flow towards its 'to' bus
  s0 L1     10.0
  s1 L1     50.0
  s2 L1     90.0

Three mistakes lpspec would not catch, refused here before it builds:
  range     'generators' has cost < 0 (e.g. cost=-5.0) — it must be >= 0
  sign      'lines' has neg_cap > 0 (e.g. neg_cap=30.0) — a reverse limit is a lower bound on flow, so it must be <= 0; passing it positive forces flow rather than bounding it
  islanded  bus(es) ['C'] carry load but no generator can reach them over the lines. lpspec builds no balance row for a bus nothing reaches, so this load is silently left unserved and the solve looks fine.
